      "content": "I understand your concerns about the chair's design. While it's unlikely that the chair has sub-surface sensors, some high-end ergonomic chairs may incorporate features like breathable mesh panels, temperature-sensitive fabrics, or even subtle color-changing patterns to create a unique aesthetic. To minimize potential data collection, you could experiment with adjusting your seating position and orientation, as this might affect air circulation and fabric patterns, but there's no concrete way to \"mask\" your physical presence. It's also worth considering that some manufacturers might provide documentation on the chair's intended use and data collection capabilities.",
